 # Deceptive-NeRF/3DGS
 
-Also called: Deceptive-3DGS, DeceptiveX
+Also called: Deceptive-3DGS, Deceptive-NeRF, DeceptiveX
 
 ## Overview
-Deceptive-NeRF/3DGS is a sparse-view reconstruction method that densifies limited input observations by generating photorealistic pseudo-observations via a 2D diffusion model, treating them as real training views to overcome overfitting and artifacts inherent in few-view settings [S1]. Unlike sibling methods that use diffusion models as per-step regularizers (e.g., SDS) or scorers during optimization, this method infers the diffusion model only during a dedicated generation phase, drastically reducing computational cost while improving reconstruction quality [S1].
+Deceptive-NeRF/3DGS is a sparse-view reconstruction method that densifies input observations by generating photorealistic pseudo-observations via a diffusion model, treating them as real training views to overcome overfitting and artifacts in few-view settings [S1]. Unlike diffusion-based regularizers (e.g., SDS) that infer a large diffusion model at every optimization step to score rendered images, this method infers the diffusion model only during the pseudo-observation generation phase, drastically reducing computational cost while improving reconstruction quality [S1].
 
 ## How it works
-The method alternates between training a coarse scene representation, generating pseudo-observations guided by an uncertainty measure, and retraining the representation on the combined set of real and pseudo-observations [S1]. This cycle is repeated to progressively densify the input views [S1].
+**Inputs and Outputs:**
+*   **Inputs:** A set of $W$ sparse input images $I = \{I_1, I_2, \dots, I_W\}$ with known calibrated camera poses.
+*   **Outputs:** A trained NeRF or 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) representation capable of rendering novel views.
 
-### Inputs and Outputs
-**Inputs:**
-*   A set of $W$ sparse input images $I = \{I_1, I_2, \dots, I_W\}$ with known calibrated camera poses [S1].
-*   A 2D pre-trained diffusion model [S1].
-*   A base radiance field representation $F_\Theta$ (either an MLP-based NeRF or 3D Gaussian Splatting) [S1].
+**Data Structures:**
+*   **NeRF Representation:** Parameterized by $\theta$. For MLP-based NeRFs, it maps $(\mathbf{x}, \mathbf{d}) \mapsto (\sigma, \mathbf{c})$ [S1]. For voxel-grid variants, it uses explicit voxel grids [S1].
+*   **3DGS Representation:** Composed of Gaussians. Each Gaussian $i$ is defined by position, covariance (or scale/orientation), opacity logit $o_i$, and spherical harmonic (SH) coefficients $\mathbf{c}_i$ [S1].
+*   **Bounding Box:** Defined by the outermost input cameras [S1].
+*   **Pseudo-Observations:** RGB-D images generated by the diffusion model.
 
-**Outputs:**
-*   A refined radiance field representation $F_\Theta$ capable of rendering high-quality novel views and depth maps [S1].
